hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1457","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi told us, Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Suleiman, meaning Ibn Al-Mughirah, told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Rifa’ah, he said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was giving a sermon, and I said: An ignorant man about religion, who does not know what his religion is. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward.” He said hello to me and left the sermon. Then a chair was brought, the legs of which were devoid of iron. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat on it and made He teaches me what God has taught him, and then he delivers his sermon standing.”"
